# Clippenguin — Google OAuth config
# Spec ref: issue.md §9 Google Cloud Setup — never commit the real client ID.
#
# 1. Create a Google Cloud project, enable Drive API.
# 2. Configure OAuth consent screen (External, drive.file scope).
# 3. Create OAuth client: Application type = Chrome Extension (or Web Application
#    for local testing), paste your extension ID when prompted.
# 4. Copy the client ID and set it here. `manifest.json` keeps a placeholder;
#    the build injects the real ID from this file.
#
# For local `vite dev` the extension runtime isn't available — auth is mocked.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
# Alternative name also read by vite.config.ts (useful if you already use GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
